            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to run out of time, then the Mandarin for to be late."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 一起",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "一起 — yìqǐ — \"together\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "三年前我们一起上学 sān nián qián wǒmen yìqǐ shàngxué — Three years ago we were at school together."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "yī changes its tone here, falling to yì before the dipping qǐ: yìqǐ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "一起 (yìqǐ) is built from 一 'one' and 起 'to rise', both inherited from Middle Chinese, 'jit and khiX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). Rising as one is a likely picture, but how the pair came to mean together is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday answers."
